WEBVTT

00:01:10.217 --> 00:01:12.050
What the?!

00:02:59.883 --> 00:03:02.150
Okay, i think i found a way

00:03:02.184 --> 00:03:04.150
We can bypass that
construction just east of here.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:07.317
We might even make pennsylvania
faster than we thought.

00:03:07.351 --> 00:03:08.751
Yeah.

00:03:08.784 --> 00:03:11.050
Problem is we're not
going to pennsylvania.

00:03:11.084 --> 00:03:13.084
Wait... what?

00:03:13.117 --> 00:03:15.517
I just got a call from an old friend.

00:03:15.551 --> 00:03:17.517
Her father was killed last night.

00:03:17.551 --> 00:03:19.050
She thinks it might
be our kind of thing.

00:03:19.084 --> 00:03:20.250
What?

00:03:20.284 --> 00:03:21.684
Yeah, believe me,

00:03:21.718 --> 00:03:25.184
<i>She never would've called,
never, if she didn't need us.</i>

00:03:27.217 --> 00:03:29.150
Come on. You coming or what?

00:03:40.384 --> 00:03:42.883
By "old friend," you mean...

00:03:42.917 --> 00:03:45.150
A friend that's not new.

00:03:45.184 --> 00:03:46.384
Yeah, thanks.

00:03:46.417 --> 00:03:49.718
So, her name's cassie, huh?

00:03:49.751 --> 00:03:51.451
You never mentioned her.

00:03:51.484 --> 00:03:53.517
Didn't i? No.

00:03:53.551 --> 00:03:56.184
Yeah, we went out. You
mean you dated someone?

00:03:56.217 --> 00:03:59.484
For more than one night?

00:03:59.517 --> 00:04:02.150
Am i speaking a language
you're not getting here?

00:04:02.184 --> 00:04:04.651
Dad and i were working
a job in athens, ohio.

00:04:04.684 --> 00:04:07.551
She was finishing up college.
We went out for a couple weeks.

00:04:07.584 --> 00:04:09.184
And?

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:14.250
Look, it's terrible about her dad,

00:04:14.284 --> 00:04:16.917
But it kind of sounds like
a standard car accident.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.217
I'm not seeing how it
fits with what we do.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.451
Which, by the way, how
does she know what we do?

00:04:26.983 --> 00:04:29.917
You told her. You told her the secret.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.917
Our big family rule number one...

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.217
We do what we do and
we shut up about it.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.850
For a year and a half, i do
nothing but lie to jessica,

00:04:36.883 --> 00:04:39.551
And you go out with this
chick in ohio a couple of times

00:04:39.584 --> 00:04:41.818
And you tell her everything?

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:42.850
Dean!

00:04:42.883 --> 00:04:44.850
Yeah, looks like.

00:04:49.417 --> 00:04:51.484
Anderson: It's a
newspaper we put out here,

00:04:51.485 --> 00:04:53.317
Not a bulletin for the mayor's office.

00:04:53.351 --> 00:04:55.117
Get off your soapbox, jimmy.

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:57.384
I'm urging a little discretion is all.

00:04:57.417 --> 00:05:00.484
No, i think you're telling
us what you want us to print

00:05:00.517 --> 00:05:02.417
And what you want us to sit on.

00:05:02.451 --> 00:05:04.217
I know you're upset, cassie.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:05.850
I liked your dad a lot.

00:05:05.883 --> 00:05:09.250
But i think your grief
is clouding your judgment.

00:05:09.284 --> 00:05:12.117
Two black people were killed
on the same stretch of road

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:13.917
In the same way in three weeks.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.718
Jimmy, you're too close to this.

00:05:15.751 --> 00:05:18.150
Those guys were friends of yours.

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:23.551
Again, i'm very sorry for your loss.

00:05:32.983 --> 00:05:35.484
Dean.

00:05:35.517 --> 00:05:37.084
Hey, cassie.

00:05:43.184 --> 00:05:45.451
This is my brother, sam.

00:05:49.217 --> 00:05:50.818
I'm sorry about your dad.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:54.718
Yeah, me, too.

00:05:58.517 --> 00:06:01.351
My mother's in pretty bad shape.

00:06:01.384 --> 00:06:03.017
I've been staying with her.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.517
I wish she wouldn't go off by herself.

00:06:05.551 --> 00:06:07.917
She's been snervous and frightened.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:09.551
She was worried about dad.

00:06:09.584 --> 00:06:10.917
Why?

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:11.950
He was scared.

00:06:11.983 --> 00:06:13.517
He was seeing things.

00:06:13.551 --> 00:06:14.818
Like what?

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:17.718
He swore he saw an awful-Looking
black truck following him.

00:06:17.751 --> 00:06:20.117
A truck? Who was the driver?

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:23.150
He didn't talk about a
driver, just the truck.

00:06:23.184 --> 00:06:25.751
He said it would appear and disappear.

00:06:25.784 --> 00:06:28.617
And in the accident,
dad's truck was dented

00:06:28.651 --> 00:06:31.751
Like it had been slammed
into by something big.

00:06:31.784 --> 00:06:32.983
Thanks.

00:06:33.017 --> 00:06:36.551
Now, you're sure this
dent wasn't there before?

00:06:36.584 --> 00:06:38.617
He sold cars, always drove a new one.

00:06:38.651 --> 00:06:40.718
There wasn't a scratch on that thing.

00:06:40.751 --> 00:06:44.551
It had rained hard that night.
There was mud everywhere.

00:06:44.584 --> 00:06:49.284
There was a distinct set of
muddy tracks from dad's car

00:06:49.317 --> 00:06:52.351
Leading right...

00:06:52.384 --> 00:06:55.351
To the edge where he went over.

00:06:56.751 --> 00:06:59.584
One set of tracks... his.

00:06:59.617 --> 00:07:02.284
And the first person killed
was a friend of your father's?

00:07:02.317 --> 00:07:03.718
Best friend... clayton solmes.

00:07:03.751 --> 00:07:05.451
They owned a car dealership together.

00:07:05.484 --> 00:07:09.351
Same thing... dent, no tracks.

00:07:09.384 --> 00:07:12.850
And the cops said exactly
what they said about dad...

00:07:12.883 --> 00:07:14.551
"He lost control of his car."

00:07:14.584 --> 00:07:16.784
Can you think of why your father
and partner might be targets?

00:07:16.818 --> 00:07:18.250
No.

00:07:18.284 --> 00:07:20.284
You think this vanishing
truck ran him off the road?

00:07:20.317 --> 00:07:24.017
When you say it aloud like that...

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:29.384
Listen, i'm a little skeptical
about this ghost stuff

00:07:29.417 --> 00:07:31.917
Or whatever it is you guys are into.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:33.451
Skeptical.

00:07:33.484 --> 00:07:35.950
If i remember, i think
you said i was nuts.

00:07:35.983 --> 00:07:37.818
That was then.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:40.117
Hmm.

00:07:42.117 --> 00:07:44.718
I just know that i can't
explain what happened up there,

00:07:44.751 --> 00:07:46.417
So i called you.

00:07:47.983 --> 00:07:50.718
Mom. Where have you been?

00:07:50.751 --> 00:07:54.784
I had no idea you'd
invited friends over.

00:07:54.818 --> 00:07:59.150
Mom, this is dean, a friend
of mine from... college,

00:07:59.184 --> 00:08:01.718
And his brother, sam.

00:08:01.751 --> 00:08:06.050
Well, l-L-L-I
won't interrupt you.

00:08:06.084 --> 00:08:07.317
Mrs. Robinson? Hmm?

00:08:07.351 --> 00:08:09.784
We're sorry for your loss.

00:08:09.818 --> 00:08:12.784
We'd like to talk to you for
a minute, if you don't mind.

00:08:12.818 --> 00:08:17.150
I'm really not up to that just now.

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:15.150
Dd: Jimmy meant something to this town.

00:09:15.184 --> 00:09:16.883
He was one of our best.

00:09:16.917 --> 00:09:19.417
It won't be the same without him.

00:09:19.451 --> 00:09:22.384
Our best seem to be dropping like flies.

00:09:22.417 --> 00:09:24.250
Clayton, my father, jimmy.

00:09:24.284 --> 00:09:27.050
What is it exactly you want me to do?

00:09:27.084 --> 00:09:31.050
Well, how about closing this
section of road for starters?

00:09:31.084 --> 00:09:33.250
Close the main road, the
only road in and out of town?

00:09:33.284 --> 00:09:37.384
Accidents happen, cassie. That's
what they are... accidents.

00:09:37.417 --> 00:09:39.818
Did the cops check for
denting on jimmy's car

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.484
To see if it was pushed?

00:09:41.517 --> 00:09:42.684
Who's this?

00:09:42.718 --> 00:09:45.651
Dean and sam winchester, family friends.

00:09:45.684 --> 00:09:48.818
This is mayor harold todd.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:52.017
There's one set of tracks...
one. Doesn't point to foul play.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.351
Mayor, the police and town officials

00:09:54.384 --> 00:09:56.117
Take their cues from you...
if you're indifferent about...

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.417
Indifferent?

00:09:57.451 --> 00:10:00.284
Would you close the road
if the victims were white?

00:10:00.317 --> 00:10:03.117
You're suggesting i'm racist, cassie.

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:06.684
I'm the last person you
should talk to like that.

00:10:06.718 --> 00:10:07.684
Why is that?

00:10:07.718 --> 00:10:09.917
Why don't you k your mother?

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:18.784
I'll say this for her... she's fearless.

00:10:18.818 --> 00:10:19.850
Mm-Hmm.

00:10:19.883 --> 00:10:23.384
Bet she kicked your ass a coupleimes.

00:10:23.417 --> 00:10:27.050
What's interesting is you guys
never really look at each other

00:10:27.084 --> 00:10:28.184
At the same time.

00:10:28.217 --> 00:10:30.651
You look at her when she's not looking.

00:10:30.684 --> 00:10:33.084
She checks you out when you look away.

00:10:34.617 --> 00:10:38.451
It's just a... just an
interesting observation

00:10:38.484 --> 00:10:42.084
In a, you know,
observationally interesting way.

00:10:42.117 --> 00:10:44.818
You think we might have some
more pressing issues here?

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:47.150
Hey, if i'm hitting a nerve...

00:10:47.184 --> 00:10:48.484
Oh, let's go.

00:11:03.451 --> 00:11:05.651
Excuse me. Are you ron stubbins?

00:11:05.684 --> 00:11:07.484
Friends with jimmy anderson?

00:11:07.517 --> 00:11:08.684
Who are you?

00:11:08.718 --> 00:11:11.317
We're with mr. Anderson's
insurance company.

00:11:11.351 --> 00:11:14.150
Just here to dot some
i's and cross some t's.

00:11:14.184 --> 00:11:16.451
We were just wondering,
had the deceased mentioned

00:11:16.484 --> 00:11:18.017
Any unusual recent experiences?

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:19.484
What do you mean, "unusual"?

00:11:19.517 --> 00:11:21.317
Well, visions, hallucinations.

00:11:21.351 --> 00:11:24.250
It's all part of a medical
examination kind of thing.

00:11:24.284 --> 00:11:26.351
What company you say you were with?

00:11:26.384 --> 00:11:28.684
All tional mutual.

00:11:28.718 --> 00:11:32.284
Tell me, did he ever
mention seeing a truck,

00:11:32.317 --> 00:11:34.284
A big black truck?

00:11:34.317 --> 00:11:36.684
What the hell you talking
about? You even speaking english?

00:11:36.718 --> 00:11:40.117
Son, this truck, a big,
scary, monster-Looking thing?

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:41.818
Yeah, actually, i think so.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.883
Hmm.

00:11:43.917 --> 00:11:45.551
What?

00:11:45.584 --> 00:11:47.184
I have heard of a truck like that.

00:11:47.217 --> 00:11:48.484
You have?

00:11:48.517 --> 00:11:49.517
Where?

00:11:49.551 --> 00:11:51.684
Not where... when.

00:11:51.718 --> 00:11:55.050
Back in the '60s, there
was a string of deaths.

00:11:55.084 --> 00:11:57.451
Black men.

00:11:57.484 --> 00:12:01.784
Stores they disappeared in
a big, nasty black truck.

00:12:01.818 --> 00:12:03.317
They ever catch the guy who did it?

00:12:03.351 --> 00:12:04.384
Never found him.

00:12:04.417 --> 00:12:09.050
Hell, not sure they even really looked.

00:12:09.084 --> 00:12:11.250
See, there was a time

00:12:11.284 --> 00:12:18.117
This town wasn't too
friendly to all its citizens.

00:12:20.484 --> 00:12:21.551
Thank you.

00:12:26.351 --> 00:12:27.351
Truck.

00:12:27.384 --> 00:12:28.818
Keeps coming up, doesn't it?

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:31.084
<i>I was thinking. You heard
of the flying dutchman?</i>

00:12:31.117 --> 00:12:33.718
Yeah, a ghost ship infused
with the captain's evil spirit.

00:12:33.751 --> 00:12:35.284
It was basically a part of him.

00:12:35.317 --> 00:12:37.451
So, what if we're dealing
with the same thing?

00:12:37.484 --> 00:12:40.250
A phantom truck who's the
extension of some bastard ghost,

00:12:40.284 --> 00:12:41.451
Re-Enacting past crimes.

00:12:41.484 --> 00:12:43.317
The victims have all been black men.

00:12:43.351 --> 00:12:44.850
I think it's more than that.

00:12:44.883 --> 00:12:47.651
They all seem connected
to cassie and her family.

00:12:47.684 --> 00:12:49.850
All right, well, you work that angle.

00:12:49.883 --> 00:12:50.917
Go talk to her.

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:52.184
Yeah, i will.

00:12:52.217 --> 00:12:54.451
Oh, and you might also want
to mention that other thing.

00:12:54.484 --> 00:12:57.017
What other thing?

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:59.983
That serious unfinished business.

00:13:00.017 --> 00:13:03.617
Dean, what is going on between you two?

00:13:03.651 --> 00:13:06.084
So maybe we were a little
bit more involved than i said.

00:13:06.117 --> 00:13:09.084
Oh, okay, yeah.

00:13:09.117 --> 00:13:11.150
Okay, a lot more... maybe.

00:13:11.184 --> 00:13:14.284
I told her the secret about
what we do, and i shouldn't have.

00:13:14.317 --> 00:13:17.284
Look, man, everybody's got to
open up to someone sometime.

00:13:17.317 --> 00:13:18.584
Yeah, i don't.

00:13:18.617 --> 00:13:21.850
It was stupid to get that
close. I mean, look how it ended.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:24.850
Would you stop?

00:13:26.751 --> 00:13:28.718
Blink or something.

00:13:28.751 --> 00:13:30.317
You loved her.

00:13:30.351 --> 00:13:31.484
Oh, god.

00:13:31.517 --> 00:13:36.050
You were in love with
her, but you dumped her.

00:13:38.451 --> 00:13:41.017
Oh, wow.

00:13:42.751 --> 00:13:44.117
She dumped you.

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:46.950
Get in the car.

00:13:46.983 --> 00:13:49.084
Get in the car!

00:14:04.284 --> 00:14:05.617
Dean.

00:14:05.651 --> 00:14:07.184
Hey. Hey.

00:14:07.217 --> 00:14:09.351
Come on in.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:15.084
So, you busy?

00:14:15.117 --> 00:14:16.617
The paper is doing a tribute to jimmy.

00:14:16.651 --> 00:14:21.651
I was just going through
his stuff, his awards,

00:14:21.684 --> 00:14:24.584
Trying to find the words.

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:28.417
That's got to be tough.

00:14:28.451 --> 00:14:30.850
For years this family owned
the paper, the dorians.

00:14:30.883 --> 00:14:32.850
They had a whites-Only staff policy.

00:14:32.883 --> 00:14:36.784
After they sold it, jimmy
became the first black reporter.

00:14:36.818 --> 00:14:39.651
He became editor.

00:14:39.684 --> 00:14:41.818
He taught me everything.

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:43.284
Where's your brother?

00:14:45.084 --> 00:14:46.384
Not here.

00:14:46.417 --> 00:14:48.584
All right, so, what brings you here?

00:14:48.617 --> 00:14:50.651
I'm trying to find the connection

00:14:50.684 --> 00:14:52.184
Between the three victims.

00:14:52.217 --> 00:14:53.684
By the way, did you talk to your mom

00:14:53.718 --> 00:14:55.751
About what todd said
about not being a racist?

00:14:55.784 --> 00:14:56.950
I did.

00:14:56.983 --> 00:15:00.250
She didn't want to talk about it.

00:15:02.784 --> 00:15:06.417
So, just then, why did you
ask where my brother was?

00:15:06.451 --> 00:15:07.850
Nothing. Not important.

00:15:07.883 --> 00:15:10.883
Could it be because without
him here it'just you and me

00:15:10.917 --> 00:15:12.751
And not you, me, and sam,
which would be easier?

00:15:12.784 --> 00:15:14.050
It's not easier.

00:15:14.084 --> 00:15:15.751
Look...

00:15:15.784 --> 00:15:18.484
No, forget it. It's fine.

00:15:18.517 --> 00:15:21.551
Keep it strictly business.

00:15:21.584 --> 00:15:24.050
I forgot you do that.

00:15:24.084 --> 00:15:26.617
Do what?

00:15:26.651 --> 00:15:29.017
Oh, whenever we get...

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:31.284
What's the word, close?...

00:15:31.317 --> 00:15:34.084
Anywhere in the neighborhood
of emotional vulnerability,

00:15:34.117 --> 00:15:36.517
You back off or make some joke

00:15:36.551 --> 00:15:38.551
Or find any way to shut the door on me.

00:15:38.584 --> 00:15:40.484
Oh, that's hilarious.

00:15:40.517 --> 00:15:43.284
See, i'm not the one who
took that big, final door

00:15:43.317 --> 00:15:45.117
And slammed it behind
me, and i'm not the one

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:46.617
Who took the key and buried it.

00:15:46.651 --> 00:15:48.351
Are we done with this metaphor?

00:15:48.384 --> 00:15:49.983
All i'm saying is i was totally
up front with you back then

00:15:50.017 --> 00:15:51.050
And you nailed me with it.

00:15:51.084 --> 00:15:53.017
The guy i'm hoping might be in my future

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.950
Tells me he professionally pops ghosts.

00:15:54.983 --> 00:15:56.384
Those weren't the words i used.

00:15:56.417 --> 00:15:58.584
And he has to leave too
work with his father. I did.

00:15:58.617 --> 00:16:00.250
All i could think was,
if you want out, fine.

00:16:00.284 --> 00:16:02.217
But don't tell me this insane story.

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:03.651
It was the truth, cassie,

00:16:03.684 --> 00:16:06.150
It didn't sound so insane the
minute you thought i could help.

00:16:06.184 --> 00:16:08.250
Back then i thought you
just wanted to dump me.

00:16:08.284 --> 00:16:11.050
Whoa, let's not forget
who dumped who, okay?

00:16:11.084 --> 00:16:13.250
I thought it was what you wanted.

00:16:13.284 --> 00:16:14.384
Well, it wasn't.

00:16:14.417 --> 00:16:16.217
I didn't mean to hurt you.

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:17.217
Well, you did.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:19.184
I'm sorry. Yeah, me, too.

00:18:21.617 --> 00:18:24.250
Absolutely.

00:18:24.283 --> 00:18:27.283
Actually, we were always
pretty good at fighting.

00:18:27.317 --> 00:18:29.784
This, we were good at.

00:18:29.817 --> 00:18:34.150
It's all the other stuff, not so much.

00:18:34.183 --> 00:18:36.917
Hey, i tried.

00:18:36.951 --> 00:18:40.984
I told you who i really was.
It was a big first for me.

00:18:41.018 --> 00:18:43.183
Why'd you tell me?

00:18:43.217 --> 00:18:45.617
I don't know.

00:18:48.617 --> 00:18:51.951
I guess i couldn't lie to you.

00:18:54.751 --> 00:18:56.817
Dean...

00:18:56.851 --> 00:19:00.384
When you told me that story,

00:19:00.417 --> 00:19:02.183
It scared the hell out of me.

00:19:02.217 --> 00:19:06.550
I thought you were nuts, dangerous even.

00:19:06.584 --> 00:19:10.183
Actually...

00:19:10.217 --> 00:19:14.517
Maybe i was looking for
a reason to walk away.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:20.250
In my work i see some horrible things,

00:19:20.283 --> 00:19:23.018
Things that can't be explained.

00:19:23.051 --> 00:19:24.450
I deal with them.

00:19:24.484 --> 00:19:27.084
But working things out with you?

00:19:27.118 --> 00:19:29.751
I'm a scary one, all right.

00:19:29.784 --> 00:19:31.317
Hmm.

00:19:37.084 --> 00:19:41.684
Well, usually thgs get worked out

00:19:41.717 --> 00:19:44.484
When you really want them to.

00:19:48.784 --> 00:19:53.150
Yeah, but i'm still really
involved in my dad's work.

00:19:55.317 --> 00:20:00.851
No more excuses, okay? From you or me.

00:20:00.884 --> 00:20:02.084
Okay.

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:22.150
Yeah

00:20:22.183 --> 00:20:25.283
You're kidding.

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.018
And he's with me.

00:20:33.018 --> 00:20:35.283
Where were you last night?

00:20:35.317 --> 00:20:38.317
You didn't make it back to the motel.

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:39.450
Nope.

00:20:39.484 --> 00:20:41.417
I'm guessing you guys worked things out.

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:43.450
We'll be working things
out when we're 90.

00:20:43.484 --> 00:20:44.751
So, what happened?

00:20:44.784 --> 00:20:47.084
Every bone crushed, internal
organs turned to pudding.

00:20:47.118 --> 00:20:48.317
The cops are all stumped,

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.217
But it's almost like
something ran him over.

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.784
Something like a truck? Yep.

00:20:51.817 --> 00:20:53.884
Tracks? Nope.

00:20:53.917 --> 00:20:55.984
What was the mayor doing here anyway?

00:20:56.018 --> 00:20:58.450
He owned the property.
Bought it a few weeks ago.

00:20:58.484 --> 00:21:00.617
Yeah, but he's white.
Doesn't fit the pattern.

00:21:00.651 --> 00:21:02.484
Killings didn't happen up on the road.

00:21:02.517 --> 00:21:05.384
That doesn't fit, either.

00:21:11.317 --> 00:21:12.584
Thanks.

00:21:12.617 --> 00:21:14.951
I'm trying to find some
link between those killings

00:21:14.984 --> 00:21:16.751
In the '60s and what's going on now.

00:21:16.784 --> 00:21:18.717
There wasn't a lot
about it in the paper.

00:21:18.751 --> 00:21:21.584
Not surprising. Probably
minimal-Police-Work deal.

00:21:21.617 --> 00:21:23.917
Back then, equal justice under the law

00:21:23.951 --> 00:21:25.851
Wasn't too literal around here.

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:29.617
Yeah?

00:21:29.651 --> 00:21:31.183
Sam: Okay, the courthouse records

00:21:31.217 --> 00:21:34.350
Show that mr. And mrs. Mayor
bought an abandoned property.

00:21:34.384 --> 00:21:36.350
The previous owner
was the dorian family,

00:21:36.384 --> 00:21:37.784
For like 150 years.

00:21:37.817 --> 00:21:39.118
Dorian? Yeah.

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:41.550
Didn't you say the dorian
family used to own this paper?

00:21:41.584 --> 00:21:43.550
Along with most everything
else around here.

00:21:43.584 --> 00:21:45.717
Real pillars of the town.

00:21:45.751 --> 00:21:47.018
Right, right.

00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:50.984
That's interesting.

00:21:51.018 --> 00:21:52.951
What?

00:21:52.984 --> 00:21:56.051
This cyrus dorian, he
vanished in april of '63.

00:21:56.084 --> 00:21:59.051
The case was investigated
but never solved.

00:21:59.084 --> 00:22:01.417
It was the time the string
of murders was going on.

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:03.118
Well, i pulled a bunch of
paper up on the dorian place.

00:22:03.150 --> 00:22:04.817
It must've been in bad shape
when the mayor bought it.

00:22:04.851 --> 00:22:06.350
Why is that?

00:22:06.384 --> 00:22:08.051
The first thing he did
was bulldoze the place.

00:22:08.084 --> 00:22:10.751
Mayor todd knocked down the dorianlace?

00:22:10.784 --> 00:22:14.450
It was a big deal. One of
the oldest local houses left.

00:22:14.484 --> 00:22:16.051
It made the front page.

00:22:16.084 --> 00:22:17.217
You got a date?

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:20.517
Uh... the 3rd of last month.

00:22:24.717 --> 00:22:28.183
Mayor todd bulldozed the
dorian family home on the 3rd.

00:22:28.217 --> 00:22:31.084
The first killing was the very next day.

00:23:53.550 --> 00:23:55.018
Dean!

00:23:59.230 --> 00:24:01.297
Maybe you could throw
a couple shots in that.

00:24:02.230 --> 00:24:05.964
You didn't see who
was driving the truck?

00:24:07.364 --> 00:24:08.764
It seemed to be no one.

00:24:11.663 --> 00:24:13.864
Everything was moving so fast.

00:24:15.567 --> 00:24:20.867
And then it was just gone.
Why didn't it kill us?

00:24:20.901 --> 00:24:24.567
Whatever is controlling the
truck wants you afraid first.

00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:29.767
Mrs. Robinson, cassie said
that your husband saw the truck

00:24:29.801 --> 00:24:32.433
Before he died.

00:24:32.467 --> 00:24:33.767
Mom?

00:24:33.801 --> 00:24:35.268
Hmm?

00:24:36.234 --> 00:24:39.101
Martin was under a lot of stress.

00:24:39.134 --> 00:24:41.101
You can't be sure about
what he was seeing.

00:24:41.134 --> 00:24:43.500
Well, after tonight i think
we can be reasonably sure

00:24:43.534 --> 00:24:44.901
That he was seeing a truck.

00:24:44.934 --> 00:24:50.234
What happened tonight, you
and cassie are marked, okay?

00:24:50.268 --> 00:24:52.600
Your daughter could die,
so if you know something,

00:24:52.634 --> 00:24:54.567
Now would be a really good
time to tell us about it.

00:24:54.600 --> 00:24:56.467
Dean... yes.

00:24:56.500 --> 00:24:59.168
Yes, he said he saw a truck.

00:24:59.201 --> 00:25:01.400
Did he know who it belonged to?

00:25:01.433 --> 00:25:03.734
He thought he did. Who was that?

00:25:05.801 --> 00:25:08.767
Cyrus...

00:25:08.801 --> 00:25:11.867
A man named cyrus.

00:25:15.201 --> 00:25:17.600
Is this cyrus?

00:25:17.634 --> 00:25:23.234
Cyrus dorian died
more than 40 years ago.

00:25:23.268 --> 00:25:27.534
How do you know he died, mrs. Robinson?

00:25:29.234 --> 00:25:31.433
The paper said he went missing.

00:25:31.467 --> 00:25:33.801
How do you know he died?

00:25:33.834 --> 00:25:37.467
We were all very young.

00:25:39.467 --> 00:25:42.333
I dated cyrus a while.

00:25:42.367 --> 00:25:45.433
I was also seeing martin,
in secret of course

00:25:45.467 --> 00:25:51.700
'Cause interracial couples
didn't go over too well then.

00:25:51.734 --> 00:25:54.234
When i broke it off with cyrus,

00:25:54.268 --> 00:25:57.168
And when he found out about martin...

00:25:57.201 --> 00:26:02.667
I don't know... he changed.

00:26:02.700 --> 00:26:08.500
His hatred... his
hatred was frightening.

00:26:08.534 --> 00:26:10.001
The string of murders.

00:26:10.034 --> 00:26:12.500
There were rumors,

00:26:12.534 --> 00:26:15.367
People of color disappearing
into some kind oa truck.

00:26:18.734 --> 00:26:21.467
Nothing was ever done.

00:26:26.767 --> 00:26:28.667
Martin and...

00:26:30.667 --> 00:26:34.967
Martin and i, we were gonna be married

00:26:35.001 --> 00:26:37.001
In that little church near here,

00:26:37.034 --> 00:26:39.934
But last minute, we decided to elope

00:26:39.967 --> 00:26:42.268
'Cause we didn't want all the attention.

00:26:42.300 --> 00:26:43.534
And cyrus?

00:26:50.268 --> 00:26:55.567
The day we set for the wedding

00:26:55.600 --> 00:27:01.134
Was the day someone
set fire to the church.

00:27:09.234 --> 00:27:14.433
There was a children's
choir practicing in there.

00:27:16.901 --> 00:27:20.034
They all died.

00:27:22.467 --> 00:27:25.034
Did the attacks stop after that?

00:27:25.067 --> 00:27:28.001
No, there was one more.

00:27:30.001 --> 00:27:34.801
One night that truck came for martin.

00:27:37.268 --> 00:27:39.734
Cyrus beat him something terrible,

00:27:44.433 --> 00:27:47.634
But martin... you see, martin got loose

00:27:47.667 --> 00:27:50.500
And he started hitting cyrus

00:27:50.534 --> 00:27:54.734
And he just kept hitting
him and hitting him.

00:28:06.001 --> 00:28:08.333
Why didn't you call the cops?

00:28:12.667 --> 00:28:15.867
This was 40 years ago.

00:28:15.901 --> 00:28:19.500
He called on his friends...

00:28:19.534 --> 00:28:21.467
Clayton, solmes, and jimmy anderson...

00:28:21.500 --> 00:28:24.834
And they put cyrus' body into the truck

00:28:24.867 --> 00:28:29.433
And then rolled it into the
swamp at the edge of his land

00:28:29.467 --> 00:28:35.967
And all three of them kept
that secret all these years.

00:28:38.001 --> 00:28:39.433
And now all three are gone.

00:28:39.467 --> 00:28:40.567
So is mayor todd.

00:28:42.333 --> 00:28:45.634
Now, he said that you of all people

00:28:45.667 --> 00:28:47.467
Would know that he is not a racist.

00:28:47.500 --> 00:28:48.534
Why would he say that?

00:28:48.567 --> 00:28:49.567
He was a good man.

00:28:49.600 --> 00:28:52.867
He was a young deputy back then,

00:28:52.901 --> 00:28:54.634
Investigating cyrus's disappearance.

00:28:54.667 --> 00:29:00.367
Once he figured out what
martin and the others had done,

00:29:00.400 --> 00:29:06.201
He he did nothing

00:29:07.867 --> 00:29:10.934
Because he also knew
what cyrus had done.

00:29:14.067 --> 00:29:15.734
Why didn't you tell me?

00:29:15.767 --> 00:29:18.433
I thought i was protecting them.

00:29:20.500 --> 00:29:25.600
And now there's no one left to protect.

00:29:25.634 --> 00:29:27.001
Yes, there is.

00:29:36.268 --> 00:29:38.367
Oh, my life was so simple.

00:29:38.400 --> 00:29:42.867
Just school, exams,

00:29:42.901 --> 00:29:46.400
Papers on polycentric cultural norms.

00:29:46.433 --> 00:29:50.333
So i guess i saved you
from a boring existence.

00:29:50.367 --> 00:29:52.534
Occasionally i miss boring.

00:29:54.300 --> 00:29:55.867
So, this killer truck...

00:29:55.901 --> 00:29:59.767
I miss conversations that didn't
start with "this killer truck."

00:29:59.801 --> 00:30:02.234
Ah...

00:30:02.268 --> 00:30:04.201
All right, well, this cyrus guy,

00:30:04.234 --> 00:30:06.867
Evil on a level that
infected even his truck.

00:30:06.901 --> 00:30:10.400
When he died, the swamp became his tomb

00:30:10.433 --> 00:30:12.767
And his spirit was dormant for 40 years.

00:30:12.801 --> 00:30:14.001
So, what woke it up?

00:30:14.034 --> 00:30:16.600
The construction on his
house or the destructi.

00:30:16.634 --> 00:30:17.734
Right.

00:30:17.767 --> 00:30:20.534
Demolition or remodeling
can awaken spirits,

00:30:20.567 --> 00:30:22.268
Make them restless.

00:30:22.300 --> 00:30:24.667
Like that theater in illinois.

00:30:24.700 --> 00:30:25.934
Yeah.

00:30:25.967 --> 00:30:27.967
And the guy who tears
down the family homestead,

00:30:28.001 --> 00:30:30.500
Harold todd, is the same guy

00:30:30.534 --> 00:30:34.067
That kept cyrus's murder
quiet and unsolved.

00:30:34.101 --> 00:30:36.268
So now his spirit is
awakened and out for blood.

00:30:36.300 --> 00:30:38.567
I guess. Who knows what
ghosts are thinking anyway.

00:30:38.600 --> 00:30:41.967
You know we're gonna have to
dredge that body from the swamp?

00:30:42.001 --> 00:30:43.600
Maman.

00:30:43.634 --> 00:30:45.967
You said it. Yeah.

00:30:46.001 --> 00:30:46.967
Hey.

00:30:47.001 --> 00:30:47.967
Hey.

00:30:48.001 --> 00:30:50.034
She's asleep.

00:30:50.067 --> 00:30:52.134
Now what?

00:30:52.168 --> 00:30:53.867
You stay put and look after her.

00:30:53.901 --> 00:30:55.967
And we'll be back.
Don't leave the house.

00:30:56.001 --> 00:30:58.201
Don't go getting all
authoritative on me.

00:30:58.234 --> 00:30:59.300
I hate it.

00:31:00.734 --> 00:31:03.467
Don't leave the house, please?

00:31:15.433 --> 00:31:18.168
You coming or what?

00:31:22.767 --> 00:31:26.367
Sam: All right, let's get her up.

00:31:27.934 --> 00:31:31.168
All right. Little more.

00:31:31.201 --> 00:31:32.433
Little more.

00:31:33.700 --> 00:31:35.901
Litt more.

00:31:35.934 --> 00:31:37.168
All right, stop.

00:31:45.801 --> 00:31:46.934
Nice.

00:31:46.967 --> 00:31:49.034
Hell yeah.

00:31:49.067 --> 00:31:50.433
Now i know what she sees in you.

00:31:50.467 --> 00:31:51.700
What?

00:31:51.734 --> 00:31:54.268
Come on, you can admit it.
You're still in love with her.

00:31:54.300 --> 00:31:55.567
Can we focus, please?

00:31:55.600 --> 00:31:57.433
I'm just saying, dean.

00:31:57.467 --> 00:31:58.467
Hold that.

00:31:58.500 --> 00:32:01.101
All right. What am i getting?

00:32:01.134 --> 00:32:02.700
Gas, flashlight. Got it, got it.

00:32:02.734 --> 00:32:04.234
All right, let's get this done.

00:32:04.268 --> 00:32:06.500
All right. Got it.

00:32:23.801 --> 00:32:25.333
All right, let's get to it.

00:32:40.901 --> 00:32:43.500
Think that'll do it?

00:32:49.333 --> 00:32:51.300
I guess not.

00:32:54.927 --> 00:32:56.827
So burning the body had
no effect on that thing?

00:32:56.860 --> 00:32:58.194
Sure it did. Now it's really pissed.

00:32:58.227 --> 00:33:00.160
But cyrus's ghost is gone, right, dean?

00:33:00.194 --> 00:33:01.960
Apparently not the part
that's fused with the truck.

00:33:02.234 --> 00:33:04.033
Where you going?

00:33:04.067 --> 00:33:06.434
Going for a little ride.
Gonna lead that thing away.

00:33:06.467 --> 00:33:08.267
That rusted piece of
crap, you got to burn it.

00:33:08.300 --> 00:33:09.901
How the hell am i supposed
to burn a truck, dean?

00:33:09.934 --> 00:33:11.767
I don't know. Figure something out.

00:33:12.141 --> 00:33:13.774
Figure something...

00:33:53.671 --> 00:33:55.838
Hey, you got to give me a minute.

00:33:55.870 --> 00:33:57.371
I don't have a minute!
What are we doing?!

00:33:57.404 --> 00:34:00.371
Uh... let me get back to you.

00:34:02.838 --> 00:34:04.371
Hey, cassie? Hey, it's sam.

00:34:04.404 --> 00:34:07.437
Okay, i need some information
and it has to be exactly right.

00:34:10.704 --> 00:34:12.404
All right, dean. This better be good!

00:34:12.437 --> 00:34:16.037
Where are you? I'm in the middle of
nowhere with a killer truck on my ass!

00:34:16.070 --> 00:34:18.270
It's like it knows i
put the torch to cyrus!

00:34:18.304 --> 00:34:19.970
Dean, listen to me. It's important.

00:34:20.003 --> 00:34:21.070
I have to know exactly where you are.

00:34:21.104 --> 00:34:23.504
Decatur road, about two
miles off the highway.

00:34:23.537 --> 00:34:25.304
Okay, headed east? Yes!

00:34:30.237 --> 00:34:33.437
Oh, you son of a bitch.

00:34:33.471 --> 00:34:34.704
Okay, uh, turn right.

00:34:41.704 --> 00:34:42.903
You make the turn?

00:34:42.937 --> 00:34:44.337
Yeah, i made the turn!

00:34:44.371 --> 00:34:46.104
Move this thing along a little faster!

00:34:46.137 --> 00:34:47.704
All right, you see a road up ahead?

00:34:47.738 --> 00:34:48.937
No!

00:34:48.970 --> 00:34:50.704
Wait, yes, i see it!

00:34:50.738 --> 00:34:52.337
Okay, turn left. What?!

00:34:59.838 --> 00:35:01.404
All right, now what?

00:35:01.437 --> 00:35:03.404
Go exactly 7/10ths of a mile and stop.

00:35:03.437 --> 00:35:06.104
Stop? Exactly 7/10ths, dean.

00:35:06.137 --> 00:35:08.504
7/10ths, 7/10ths.

00:35:37.970 --> 00:35:40.804
Dean, are you still there?

00:35:40.838 --> 00:35:42.504
Yeah. What's happening?

00:35:42.537 --> 00:35:44.504
It's just staring at me. What do i do?

00:35:44.537 --> 00:35:46.903
Just what you are doing...
bringing it to you.

00:35:46.937 --> 00:35:48.003
Wh...

00:36:05.070 --> 00:36:06.604
Come on, come on.

00:36:26.637 --> 00:36:29.304
Dean?

00:36:29.337 --> 00:36:30.537
You still there?

00:36:30.571 --> 00:36:33.404
Dean?

00:36:33.437 --> 00:36:35.838
Where'd it go?

00:36:35.870 --> 00:36:39.070
Dean, you're where the church was.

00:36:39.104 --> 00:36:40.337
What church?

00:36:40.371 --> 00:36:42.838
The place cyrus burned down
and murdered all those kids.

00:36:42.870 --> 00:36:44.471
There's not a whole lot left.

00:36:44.504 --> 00:36:46.204
Church ground is hallowed ground

00:36:46.237 --> 00:36:47.738
Whether the church
is still there or not.

00:36:47.771 --> 00:36:49.804
Evil spirits cross over hallowed ground,

00:36:49.838 --> 00:36:51.571
Sometimes they're destroyed.

00:36:51.604 --> 00:36:56.504
So i figured maybe that
would get rid of it.

00:36:56.537 --> 00:36:57.537
Maybe?

00:36:57.571 --> 00:36:58.870
Maybe?!

00:36:58.903 --> 00:37:01.604
What if you were wrong?!

00:37:03.371 --> 00:37:06.070
Honestly, that thought
hadn't occurred to me.

00:37:10.270 --> 00:37:12.571
"Well, that honestly
didn't occur to me."

00:37:18.571 --> 00:37:20.237
I'm gonna kill him.

00:37:27.224 --> 00:37:30.257
My mother says to tell you thanks again.

00:37:35.190 --> 00:37:38.091
This was a better goodbye
than the last time.

00:37:38.124 --> 00:37:40.058
Yeah, well, maybe this time

00:37:40.091 --> 00:37:42.357
It'll be a little less permanent.

00:37:42.390 --> 00:37:45.957
You know what?

00:37:45.991 --> 00:37:48.991
I'm a realist.

00:37:49.024 --> 00:37:51.957
I don't see much hope for us, dean.

00:37:55.624 --> 00:37:58.490
Well, i've seen stranger things happen.

00:37:58.524 --> 00:38:00.190
Hell of a lot stranger.

00:38:04.857 --> 00:38:06.724
Goodbye, dean.

00:38:06.757 --> 00:38:09.724
I'll see you, cassie.

00:38:09.757 --> 00:38:12.691
I will.

00:39:05.257 --> 00:39:07.357
I like her.

00:39:07.390 --> 00:39:08.724
Yeah.

00:39:11.058 --> 00:39:12.824
You meet someone like her,

00:39:12.857 --> 00:39:15.657
Ever make you wonder if it's worth it...

00:39:15.691 --> 00:39:19.791
Putting everything else
on hold, doing what we do?

00:39:32.357 --> 00:39:35.457
Why don't you wake me up
when it's my turn to drive?

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.250
